From f0a4928258211a996ecbd0073bbfeb05da32c7ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 15:55:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(view): settle floating drops into frame at release, never
 on focus
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A floating window dragged mostly out of frame stayed at the extreme
position after the drop, and some later focus change flashed it to the
grabbable margin with no animation: clicking a tiled window runs the
strip reveal's arrange, and Workspace::applyPositions clamped every
floating window in passing. Both moments are wrong — the correction
belongs to the drop, and it belongs in motion.

The free drop in Cursor::finishFloatMove now settles the window into
the grabbable margin (clampFloatingOrigin + keepTitleBarReachable, the
policy floatingClampTarget encodes) with animateTo, exactly at release,
and remembers the settled origin. The drop is the only settle: the
arrange clamp in applyPositions now re-enforces the margin only when
the usable area that bounds it changed, so no arrange driven by focus,
a window opening, or a reflow repositions a floating window. Out-of-
margin states cannot otherwise persist — drops settle, rule placement
and keybind moves clamp — so the margin holds by construction.

An audit of that invariant found two restore paths it did not cover.
Fractional restores (restoreFloatingPosition, the displaced-output
restore, and the snap restore in finishFloatMove) resolve
proportionally and can land outside the margin on a smaller output —
a scale jump can leave the window fully off. They now place through
View::grabbableOrigin (keepTitleBarReachable of clampFloatingOrigin
for the frame), and the clamped origin — where the window actually is
— is what gets re-anchored. And clampFloatingPosition no longer spends
the usable-change check on an in-flight tween: mid-animation it clamps
the tween target and retargets with animateTo, instead of skipping and
letting a stale target settle out of frame.

Validated red-first on drag/floating_release_settle.sh (pixel-sampled
under a frozen clock: the settle interpolates the visible sliver
11 -> 19 -> 51 -> 75 px across the 2000 ms linear timeline, the final
box keeps floatingKeepVisible inside the usable area, and a focus
change moves nothing); mutation-proven (no settle -> red, flash
instead of animate -> slivers 75 -> 75 -> 75 -> 75 red). The arrange
gate is structural: the harness cannot distinguish it post-settle
because the margin invariant makes its input state unreachable.

The audit follow-ups are pinned by two new red-first checks.
layout/floating_cross_output_clamp.sh: a 400x300 float parked at the
source margin restores at 1883,323 onto a scale-2 output where the
margin asks for x <= 1845, y <= 285. layout/floating_clamp_retarget.sh:
a 40px exclusive panel mapping mid-tween settles at y = -225 where the
new margin asks y >= -185. Each fix is mutation-attributed: dropping
the restore clamp reddens only the first, skipping the tween retarget
reddens only the second.

Full harness suite 374/379 — the 5 failures (animation/drag_toggle,
animation/tiled_close_configure_barrier, effect/selection,
output/two_output_containment, render/title_bar_blur_refocus)
reproduce identically on a stashed base build. Meson units 139/139.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
